{"text": " ChatGPT is a flexible writing workspace for longer structured writing tasks. Instead of drafting in one tool and editing in another, you can start with a prompt in chat, build a draft quickly, and then refine its step-by-step in the same flow. There are a few ways writing typically begins. You might start with a blank prompt and ask ChatGPT to draft something from scratch. You might paste in rough notes and ask it to turn them into a memo, article, or brief. Or you might upload a document and ask ChatGPT to rewrite, summarize, or restructure it for a different audience. However you start, the workflow is the same. Give ChatGPT a clear brief, review the first draft, and improve it through targeted revisions. In this demo, I'm going to start by prompting ChatGPT. Create a one-pager for my leadership team that highlights the key insights from the attached report and how they apply to us as an AI transformation partner. The purpose is to decide how we should position ourselves based on the report's findings. Stick to the facts and make it sound like me. Once the draft appears, I don't need to start over or rewrite the whole prompt. I can choose edit at the top left corner of the draft or expand the draft window to edit directly. After scanning through the whole document, I can ask ChatGPT to adjust the text to my preference. For example, here I highlight all the text and ask, make this more concrete for a senior leadership audience. ChatGPT now edits the document to my request. I can also pick out a passage that needs adjustment and ask, shorten this by 30% and make the opening more decisive. Finally, I can do one big rewrite like turn this into a one-page decision brief with options, risks, and a clear recommendation. Now the structure updates, but the core content stays anchored to what I already approved. And that's how you can use ChatGPT to support with your writing. You're not asking for a full rewrite every time. You're improving a draft you already mostly like. And now a few practical notes. This writing capability is available on all ChatGPT plans. You can draft, edit, and refine content directly in chat. And for longer projects on the web, use the focused writing view and save documents to your library. The biggest difference between plans is the models you can access. On the free plan, you can use ChatGPT standard models, but access to more advanced models is limited. For more demanding writing tasks, access to these advanced models can often produce better results.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 5.0, "text": " ChatGPT is a flexible writing workspace for longer structured writing tasks.", "tokens": [50364, 27503, 38, 47, 51, 307, 257, 11358, 3579, 32706, 337, 2854, 18519, 3579, 9608, 13, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1649322509765625, "compression_ratio": 1.6618705035971224, "no_speech_prob": 0.0029425681568682194}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 5.4, "end": 8.700000000000001, "text": " Instead of drafting in one tool and editing in another,", "tokens": [50634, 7156, 295, 46378, 294, 472, 2290, 293, 10000, 294, 1071, 11, 50799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1649322509765625, "compression_ratio": 1.6618705035971224, "no_speech_prob": 0.0029425681568682194}, {"id": 2, "seek": 0, "start": 8.700000000000001, "end": 10.700000000000001, "text": " you can start with a prompt in chat,", "tokens": [50799, 291, 393, 722, 365, 257, 12391, 294, 5081, 11, 50899], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1649322509765625, "compression_ratio": 1.6618705035971224, "no_speech_prob": 0.0029425681568682194}, {"id": 3, "seek": 0, "start": 10.700000000000001, "end": 12.1, "text": " build a draft quickly,", "tokens": [50899, 1322, 257, 11206, 2661, 11, 50969], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1649322509765625, "compression_ratio": 1.6618705035971224, "no_speech_prob": 0.0029425681568682194}, {"id": 4, "seek": 0, "start": 12.1, "end": 15.1, "text": " and then refine its step-by-st